the <strong>longest palindromic substring</strong> within a given string.</=
p><h4 id=3D"example">Example:</h4><pre><code class=3D"hljs language-python"=
>Input: s =3D <span class=3D"hljs-string">'abccbaba'</span>
Output: <span class=3D"hljs-string">'abccba'</span>
</code></pre></div>
<h2 id=3D"intuition">Intuition</h2>
<p>A naive solution to this problem is to check every possible substring an=
d save the longest palindrome found. It takes approximately <span class=3D"=
katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/M=
ath/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><msup><=
mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><annotation e=
ncoding=3D"application/x-tex">O(n^2)</annotation></semantics></math></span>=
<span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base"><span =
class=3D"strut" style=3D"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em"></span><sp=
an class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right:0.02778em">O</span><span=
 class=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mord"><span class=3D"mord mathnorma=
l">n</span><span class=3D"msupsub"><span class=3D"vlist-t"><span class=3D"v=
list-r"><span class=3D"vlist" style=3D"height:0.8141em"><span style=3D"top:=
-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em"><span class=3D"pstrut" style=3D"height:2.7em"=
></span><span class=3D"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class=3D"mord=
 mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span cla=
ss=3D"mclose">)</span></span></span></span> time to generate all substrings=
 for a string of length <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml">=
<math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</=
mi></mrow><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">n</annotation></semant=
ics></math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span cla=
ss=3D"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height:0.4306em"></span><span cl=
ass=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span></span>, and for each of thes=
e substrings, it takes <span class=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><=
math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</m=
i><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mro=
w><annotation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics><=
/math></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D=
"base"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em"></=
span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right:0.02778em">O</sp=
an><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal">n</span><s=
pan class=3D"mclose">)</span></span></span></span> time to check if it=E2=
=80=99s a palindrome. This results in an overall time complexity of <span c=
lass=3D"katex"><span class=3D"katex-mathml"><math xmlns=3D"http://www.w3.or=
g/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy=3D"false">(</mo=
><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy=3D"false">)</mo></mrow><anno=
tation encoding=3D"application/x-tex">O(n^3)</annotation></semantics></math=
></span><span class=3D"katex-html" aria-hidden=3D"true"><span class=3D"base=
"><span class=3D"strut" style=3D"height:1.0641em;vertical-align:-0.25em"></=
span><span class=3D"mord mathnormal" style=3D"margin-right:0.02778em">O</sp=
an><span class=3D"mopen">(</span><span class=3D"mord"><span class=3D"mord m=
athnormal">n</span><span class=3D"msupsub"><span class=3D"vlist-t"><span cl=
ass=3D"vlist-r"><span class=3D"vlist" style=3D"height:0.8141em"><span style=
=3D"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em"><span class=3D"pstrut" style=3D"heigh=
t:2.7em"></span><span class=3D"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class=
=3D"mord mtight">3</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><=
